(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[15 1 "// The module _hmac (py-design-1122): Modules/hmacmodule.c of CPython 3.14.10, its HACL* streaming HMAC replaced by"] [16 1 "// RFC 2104 over Go's crypto and hashlib_blake2.go (as builtins_hashlib.go replaces HACL*'s hash functions): hmac.py"] [17 1 "// takes it for a str digestmod (HMAC._init_builtin_hmac, hmac.digest through compute_digest) when _hashlib does not"] [18 1 "// import, and test_hmac's Builtin* classes run on it. Its names: new(key, msg=None, digestmod=None), the type"] [19 1 "// _hmac.HMAC (copy, update, digest, hexdigest; name \"hmac-\" and the hash's hashlib name, digest_size, block_size;"] [20 1 "// DISALLOW_INSTANTIATION; repr \"<NAME HMAC object @ ADDRESS>\"), compute_digest(key, msg, digest) and the one-shot"] [21 1 "// compute_md5 ... compute_blake2b_32(key, msg, /), UnknownHashError (a ValueError) and _GIL_MINSIZE. The hash table:"] [22 1 "// py_hmac_static_hinfo's names and hashlib names (find_hash_info: the name, else its lower(); a digestmod that is no str"] [23 1 "// is unknown, \"unsupported hash type: %R\"); the buffers by hashlib.h's GET_BUFFER_VIEW_OR_ERROR (hashBuffer)."] [25 1 "// hmacInfo is a py_hmac_hinfo: the HACL name, the hashlib name it displays, the sizes and the hash state's constructor"] [26 1 "// (builtins_hashlib.go's pyHash, whose Go hashes goi's table knows: a hash.Hash called through an interface of the runtime's"] [27 1 "// own fails under goi, \"cannot call Write on *sha256.Digest: the type is not in the table\")."] [59 1 "// hmacTable is the module's hinfo_table: each entry by its name and its hashlib name."] [75 1 "// hmacObject is an HMACObject: the hash's information and the inner and outer states (RFC 2104)."] [78 21 "// _hashlib.HMAC's (builtins_hashopenssl.go), else _hmac.HMAC"] [90 1 "// clone is Hacl_Streaming_HMAC_copy (HMAC_CTX_copy): both states copied."] [105 1 "// hmacUnknown is the module's UnknownHashError, made once (a module per interpreter shares it)."] [120 1 "// hmacFind is find_hash_info: a str by its UTF-8 name, else by name.lower(); anything else unknown."] [147 1 "// hmacNew is _hacl_hmac_state_new: the key hashed when longer than a block, padded with zeros, the inner state fed"] [148 1 "// key ^ ipad and the outer key ^ opad."] [168 1 "// digest is Hacl_Streaming_HMAC_digest: the outer state, cloned, fed the inner state's digest."] [180 1 "// hmacOneShot is Py_HMAC_HACL_ONESHOT: the key's buffer, then the message's, then the digest."] [199 1 "// hmacArgs is clinic's _PyArg_UnpackKeywords for names that are all positional-or-keyword, the first required ones"] [200 1 "// required; nil for an absent optional one."] [320 25 "// _PyArg_CheckPositional(name, nargs, 2, 2)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[122 24] [123 32] [134 28] [135 34] [224 47] [245 49] [255 52] [317 33]] :go/trails [[56 58]]} (go/file "builtins_hmac.go" :imports [


